From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mitsuru Oshima <oshima@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:11:30 -0700
Subject: views: Defer MenuRunnerImpl destruction when released in OnMenuClosed

MenuRunnerImpl::OnMenuClosed cleared `controller_` before invoking
ExecuteCommand and OnMenuClosed on the MenuDelegate. When a delegate
reset its MenuRunner inside those callbacks while MenuController frames
were active on the stack, MenuRunnerImpl::Release saw a null
`controller_` and deleted `this` synchronously instead of calling
DeferMenuRunnerDestruction, causing a UAF on MenuItemView.

Keep the `controller_` WeakPtr across OnMenuClosed and invalidate
`weak_factory_` when deferring destruction in Release.

Bug: 574516887
TAG=agy
CONV=cced0104-bc4a-465a-9306-2ed8a06093b5

Change-Id: I948b7f6217c4ca2c93d604d689b8f34c8d2dee30
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8613791
Reviewed-by: Thomas Lukaszewicz <tluk@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Mitsuru Oshima <oshima@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1722585}

diff --git a/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_runner_impl.cc b/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_runner_impl.cc
index 5636a2be48d81470f89414cf13e6cc408fcdbb13..36d21d2c9658cbc1d4244c1063f52289db991dd3 100644
--- a/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_runner_impl.cc
+++ b/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_runner_impl.cc
@@ -110,6 +110,9 @@ void MenuRunnerImpl::Release() {
 
   bool is_stack_active = controller_ && controller_->IsStackActive();
   if (is_stack_active) {
+    // Invlidate the menu runner's weakptrs now because the menu runner is
+    // considered deleted at this point.
+    weak_factory_.InvalidateWeakPtrs();
     // Transfer ownership to controller.
     controller_->DeferMenuRunnerDestruction(base::WrapUnique(this));
     return;
@@ -264,7 +267,6 @@ void MenuRunnerImpl::OnMenuClosed(NotifyType type,
     return;
   }
   running_ = false;
-  controller_ = nullptr;
   if (menu_->GetDelegate()) {
     // Executing the command may also delete this.
     base::WeakPtr<MenuRunnerImpl> ref(weak_factory_.GetWeakPtr());
